  "units": [
    {
      "ancestors": [],
      "attributes": [
        {
          "doc_text": " A wrapper around a raw non-null `*mut T` that indicates that the possessor",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            214,
            292
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " of this wrapper owns the referent. Useful for building abstractions like",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            293,
            369
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " `Box<T>`, `Vec<T>`, `String`, and `HashMap<K, V>`.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            370,
            424
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            425,
            428
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Unlike `*mut T`, `Unique<T>` behaves \"as if\" it were an instance of `T`.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            429,
            505
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " It implements `Send`/`Sync` if `T` is `Send`/`Sync`. It also implies",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            506,
            578
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " the kind of strong aliasing guarantees an instance of `T` can expect:",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            579,
            652
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " the referent of the pointer should not be modified without a unique path to",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            653,
            732
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " its owning Unique.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            733,
            755
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            756,
            759
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " If you're uncertain of whether it's correct to use `Unique` for your purposes,",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            760,
            842
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " consider using `NonNull`, which has weaker semantics.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            843,
            900
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            901,
            904
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Unlike `*mut T`, the pointer must always be non-null, even if the pointer",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            905,
            982
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " is never dereferenced. This is so that enums may use this forbidden value",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            983,
            1060
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " as a discriminant -- `Option<Unique<T>>` has the same size as `Unique<T>`.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1061,
            1139
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " However the pointer may still dangle if it isn't dereferenced.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1140,
            1206
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1207,
            1210
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Unlike `*mut T`, `Unique<T>` is covariant over `T`. This should always be correct",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1211,
            1296
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " for any type which upholds Unique's aliasing requirements.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1297,
            1359
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": null,
          "path": "unstable",
          "range": [
            1360,
            1565
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": null,
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1566,
            1580
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": null,
          "path": "repr",
          "range": [
            1581,
            1601
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        }
